Assertions:
[DOM] the More menu entry for the module reads "Returns" {SPEC}
[BLADE] the Returns list opens without an error toast, with a status filter and a grid {OBSERVED}
[FORM] "Return module" reads ON for the store {SPEC}
[FORM] "Return email notifications" and "Return push notifications" both read ON {SPEC}
[EVIDENCE] BLOCKED guard: any miss here is an environment prerequisite - module absent, "Return module" OFF, a notification switch OFF, FileUpload:Scopes without return-attachments - and the whole suite is reported BLOCKED naming it, never FAIL.

[GRID] the return appears in the list with status Requested {SPEC}
[BLADE] the return blade shows the order number @td(RETURNS_AUTH_JOURNEY.orderNumber) and the buyer as customer {SPEC}
[DOM] the Line items blade shows requested quantity 2 for the line {SPEC}
[DOM] the reason NoLongerNeeded and the reason comment typed in SETUP are visible on the line {SPEC}
[DOM] the uploaded attachment is listed on the line and opens/downloads {SPEC}
[STATE] no decision is recorded yet: approved quantity is 0 and the line state is Requested {SPEC}

[BLADE] the return status reads "Approved" {SPEC}
[DOM] the line shows approved quantity 1 and line state Approved {SPEC}
[GRID] the Returns list row for this RMA reads Approved {SPEC}
[STATE] the decision persists after reopening the return {SPEC}
[EVIDENCE] The ticket does not specify a confirmation step for the one-click Approve (the approved field is pre-filled with the requested quantity); nothing here asserts one, and nothing asserts a hint when Approved exceeds the requested quantity (UI rework planned) - the server refusal for that case is RET-AUTH-001.

[BLADE] the return status reads "PartiallyApproved" {SPEC}
[DOM] the line shows requested 2 and approved 1, line state Approved {SPEC}
[STATE] the second requested unit is returnable again: xAPI returnableItems for line B shows one unit more than if the whole request were still held {SPEC}

[BLADE] the return status reads Rejected {SPEC}
[DOM] the line shows approved 0, line state Rejected and the decline reason entered {SPEC}
[STATE] line B returnable quantity (xAPI as the buyer) equals the value before SETUP: nothing stays held {SPEC}

[FORM] the "Approve / decline" action is not offered again for the decided line {SPEC}
[FORM] a change of the line quantity is refused on Save with a message naming that the quantity cannot be changed, or the field is read-only; the stored quantity is unchanged {OBSERVED}
[STATE] approved quantity, line state and decline reason are unchanged after any attempt {SPEC}
[STATE] the edited price is persisted after Save and reopen {OBSERVED}

[FORM] while Requested the dropdown offers "Cancelled" exactly once and never the legacy spelling "Canceled" {SPEC PO}
[FORM] while Requested it offers neither Processing nor Completed {OBSERVED}
[FORM] after the decision (Rejected) the dropdown offers no earlier status (Draft, New, Requested) and no other decision status (Approved, PartiallyApproved) {SPEC}
[FORM] in both states the options equal the endpoint list, each value once {SPEC}

[BLADE] the status reads Cancelled after Save and reopen {SPEC}
[STATE] line B returnable quantity (xAPI as the buyer) equals the value before SETUP {SPEC}
[FORM] "Approve / decline" is no longer offered {SPEC}
[STATE] the buyer sees the return as Cancelled in /account/returns {SPEC}

[BLADE] the return and its Line items (quantity, reason, attachments) are readable {SPEC}
[FORM] no "Approve / decline" action is shown, or it is disabled with no way to confirm a decision {SPEC}
[STATE] the return status still reads "Requested" afterwards {SPEC}

[GRID] each filter shows only returns whose status column equals the chosen status {SPEC}
[GRID] the displayed total equals the number of rows across pages {SPEC}
[GRID] clearing the filter restores the full list {SPEC}
[STATE] the statuses offered by the filter include the Step-2 statuses (Requested, Approved, PartiallyApproved, Rejected) {SPEC}

[DOM] the menu entry, list columns, status values, the Line items blade and the Approve / decline blade are translated {SPEC}
[NEG] no text on these screens equals a raw translation key such as "RETURN.BLADES.TITLE" {SPEC}
[DOM] the store setting group names and labels under "Return" are translated or fall back to English as whole labels, never as raw keys {SPEC}

[FORM] "Return > Return" lists: "Return module", "Order statuses allowing returns", "Return reasons", "Reasons requiring a comment", "Photos or documents required", "Return number template", "Return window, days", "Shipment statuses counted as delivered" {OBSERVED}
[FORM] "Return > Notifications" lists: "Return email notifications" and "Return push notifications" {OBSERVED}
[FORM] "Return module" and the two notification switches are toggles; "Return window, days" is numeric {OBSERVED}
